== FFM downcall price, SECONDARY arm, preview API on JDK 21 ==
java.version=21.0.10
core=/home/user/ArmoniK.Api/ffi/poc/java/core/target/release/libak_core_java.so  sink=147999962000000

A JDK 22 API measured on JDK 21 as a preview, because this container has no
JDK 22 and the proxy does not reach a JDK distributor. README 5: FFM is a
secondary arm and never a target, and R7: a ratio between two BINDING
MECHANISMS is not a ratio between ABI shapes.

  downcall               min 12.504  med 12.723  max 14.691 ns
  downcall isTrivial()   min  6.167  med  6.237  max  8.146 ns

`isTrivial()` tells the linker the call will not block, upcall or trap, so
it may skip the thread-state transition. A codec entry point that makes
reverse calls is NOT trivial and may not use it, which is why both are here:
the cheap number is the one a bulk-bytes path could have and the dear one is
what the element entry points would pay.

== the same machine's JNI prices on the SAME JDK (21), for the comparison R7 allows ==
